<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 December, from 558 to 1947.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chlothar-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">558 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,468 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Childebert's death leaves Chlothar I king of all the Franks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Childebert died after a long illness without heirs, allowing his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> to reunite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdom</a>, as their father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis I</a> had done, and to seize Childebert's treasure. The realm was divided again among Chlothar's sons in 561.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1299">1299 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">727 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ghazan's Mongols defeat the Mamluks at Wadi al-Khaznadar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> ruler Ghazan, joined by King Hethum II of Armenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>, defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, the only major Mongol victory in their long conflict. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> surrendered soon after, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> made no lasting gains.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wadi-al-khaznadar">Battle of Wadi al-Khaznadar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1598">1598 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">428 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mapuche warriors kill Governor Martín García Óñez de Loyola at Curalaba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In southern Chile, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> warriors under Pelantaro ambushed and killed the Spanish governor Martín García Óñez de Loyola and his escort. The victory set off a general uprising that destroyed the Spanish towns south of the Biobío river.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-curalaba">Battle of Curalaba</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1688">1688 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">338 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James II flees England in the Glorious Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King James II, the last Catholic monarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland, fled England after William of Orange landed with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> army in November. Parliament offered the crown to his daughter Mary II and her husband William III.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-england">William III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington resigns his military command</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> State House at Annapolis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> returned his commission to Congress. A victorious general giving up power voluntarily set a lasting precedent for civilian control of the military.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jane Austen's Emma is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Murray published Emma, though its title page bore the date 1816. Austen's comedy of a confident young matchmaker is often judged her most accomplished novel.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1888">1888 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">138 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vincent van Gogh cuts off part of his ear</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a quarrel with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-gauguin">Paul Gauguin</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vincent-van-gogh">Vincent van Gogh</a> cut off part of his left ear. Months later he entered the asylum at Saint-Rémy, where he painted The Starry Night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bell Labs demonstrates the transistor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Bardeen and Walter Brattain showed colleagues at Bell Laboratories their point-contact transistor amplifying a signal. Transistors replaced vacuum tubes and made modern electronics possible.</p></div></li></ol>
